3. Reused code and adapted data

skills/writer/scripts/_markdown.py and _repeats.py are adapted from
ilyautov/humanizer-ru, commit 3621b1ca6b9a2f84f28f692222470dc25706255d,
skills/humanizer-ru/scripts/humanizer_metrics/markdown.py and repeats.py.
Copyright and MIT permission are preserved in skills/writer/licenses/ilyautov-MIT.txt,
including when the skill folder is distributed separately.
Changes: Writer masks only closed code, keeps quotes and URLs visible,
handles nested inline backtick lengths, extends phrase repeats to English,
and resolves observed repeats back to text locations in _observations.py.
The upstream score and author-origin verdict are not used.

Contextual observation families also draw on smixs/humanizer-ru (ff990df),
Aboudjem/humanizer-skill (a58df06), and blader/humanizer (0ef9fe5).
The questions and examples are Writer's own. No donor before/after examples
are embedded as instructions to invent facts, change voice or meet a score.
